# R6 Test: Single-argument processExceptions elimination

Tests that when a variable has exactly one exception tree (a Node with a
single exception subtree), the generated Lean4 code does NOT wrap the call
in `processExceptions [...]`. Instead, the single exception call is used
directly in the match expression.

## Before R6 (Lean4 output):

```
-- For the exception_result variable:
def SingleExceptionScope_exception_result_tree_0_exception_0 ... : Option Int :=
  if (x > 100) then some (x + 999) else none

def SingleExceptionScope_exception_result_tree_0 ... : Option Int :=
  (match processExceptions [SingleExceptionScope_exception_result_tree_0_exception_0 ...]
    with | none => some (x + 1) | some r => some r)
```

## After R6 (Lean4 output):

```
-- processExceptions wrapper removed, single call used directly:
def SingleExceptionScope_exception_result_tree_0_exception_0 ... : Option Int :=
  if (x > 100) then some (x + 999) else none

def SingleExceptionScope_exception_result_tree_0 ... : Option Int :=
  (match SingleExceptionScope_exception_result_tree_0_exception_0 ...
    with | none => some (x + 1) | some r => some r)
```

## Multi-exception case (should still use processExceptions):

```
-- multi_exception_result has 2 exceptions, so processExceptions is preserved:
def MultiExceptionScope_multi_exception_result_tree_0 ... : Option Int :=
  (match processExceptions [exception_0_call, exception_1_call]
    with | none => some (x + 1) | some r => some r)
```

```catala
declaration scope SingleExceptionScope:
  input x content integer
  output exception_result content integer

scope SingleExceptionScope:
  definition exception_result equals x + 1

  exception definition exception_result equals
    if x > 100 then x + 999
    else x + 1

declaration scope MultiExceptionScope:
  input x content integer
  output multi_exception_result content integer

scope MultiExceptionScope:
  definition multi_exception_result equals x + 1

  exception definition multi_exception_result equals
    if x > 100 then x + 999
    else x + 1

  exception definition multi_exception_result equals
    if x > 200 then x + 9999
    else x + 1
```
